  "verdict": "SHIPPED, narrowly. With district rainfall joined, the model scores 50.08% MAPE against 59.25% for persistence and 61.44% for the historical mean \u2014 it beats both by 15.5%. An ablation on the IDENTICAL test split shows rainfall itself is worth 4.46 points (8.2%); the model beat persistence without it too, so the earlier \"no signal without rainfall\" conclusion was partly an artifact of the old 2012-2017 test window. Only 5 of 21 crops are actually served: beating a bad baseline is not enough, so a crop must ALSO come in under 40% MAPE. Safflower beat its baselines at 101% MAPE and is withheld.",
